## Rule Maintenance

### When to Create a New Rule

Create a new rule when:
- ✅ You discover a recurring pattern or issue
- ✅ There's a common mistake that needs prevention
- ✅ You learn something that would have saved time earlier
- ✅ A feature has specific conventions not obvious from code

Don't create a rule when:
- ❌ It's a one-time fix
- ❌ It's already covered in existing documentation
- ❌ It's self-evident from the code structure

### When to Update Existing Rules

Update rules when:
- ✅ You discover the root cause of a previously documented issue
- ✅ A better pattern or solution emerges
- ✅ The existing rule is incomplete or misleading
- ✅ Framework/library conventions change

### Version Control

- Commit rule changes with clear messages explaining what changed and why
- When significantly revising a rule, consider keeping the old content in a "Legacy Notes" section
- Reference specific commits or PRs that relate to the rule

